  "geometric_reason": "With Q.T@Q=I and the binary ReLU mask M, J_C=Q.T@(I-2M)@Q, hence J_C.T@J_C=I almost everywhere at orthogonal initialization. This preserves local backward gradient norms inside the CPL trunk at initialization, not global pairwise distances or gradients for all later training steps.",
